  ],
  "text": "Nothing is pulling you toward the ground right now. Every pull you have ever felt had something in between. But Earth touches nothing, and the Moon has circled it for four billion years. Because mass does not tug on space. It dents it. Stretch a bedsheet, drop a bowling ball in, and the whole sheet sags. Roll a marble past it and the marble curves, though nothing ever touched it. And this is the part a pull could never explain. Light has no weight, and gravity still bends it. A rope only moves what it can grab. A bent road bends everyone. So you are not being pulled down. You are falling, and the ground is in the way. Take the ground away, and you would simply keep missing it. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
